  plain: `LangGraph lets you draw your agent\'s process as a flowchart in code: steps, decisions and loops, with a shared notebook of state. Because you define the flow, it is easier to add approvals, retries and reliable resumption than in a free-form agent.`,
  technical: `Core concepts commonly described: state schema, nodes (functions/agents), edges and conditional routing, reducers for state updates, persistence via checkpointers, interrupts for human-in-the-loop, and streaming. It is developed by the LangChain team but can be used without LangChain components. APIs and product tiers evolve; check current docs.`,
